{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Command the children of Israel.</b> This is the section of the command of the lamps. And the section ״וְאַתָּה תְּצַוֶּה״ was said only in the order of the work of the Tabernacle, to explain the requirement of the Menorah — and so it implies: you are ultimately to command the children of Israel concerning this." "<b>Pure olive oil.</b> Three oils come forth from the olive; the first is called זָךְ. They are spelled out in Menachot (86a) and in Tosefta Kippurim." "<b>Continually.</b> From night to night — like עֹלַת תָּמִיד, which is only from day to day."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:03.665147857Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}